    "pub_date": "2026-05-10",
    "tags": [
      "experimental",
      "weird",
      "progressive",
      "avant-garde",
      "jazz",
      "improvisation",
      "guitar"
    ],
    "excerpt": "Ava Mendoza is simply one of the best guitarists around today. She has played with a murderer's row of improvisers and experimentalists over the last 20 years, across styles incorporating rock, blues, jazz, bluegrass, metal, and the avant-garde. Alive Alone, Alive Together collects Mendoza's recent live recordings from four different events. These are matter-of-fact guitar heroics without any sense of ego. Or restraint.",
    "site_id": "avantmusicnews",
    "crawl_status": "success"
  },
  {
    "album": "Cartographies of the Unseen",
    "artist": "Vyormouth",
    "score": null,
    "url": "https://avantmusicnews.com/2026/05/09/amn-reviews-vyormouth-cartographies-of-the-unseen-2026-zerok/",
    "source": "avantmusicnews",
    "pub_date": "2026-05-09",
    "tags": [
      "experimental",
      "weird",
      "progressive",
      "avant-garde",
      "drone",
      "ambient",
      "dark"
    ],
    "excerpt": "On Cartographies of the Unseen, Vyormouth explores hidden, buried, or abandoned places in frozen settings, and asks something different of the listener. Across more than three hours of slow-moving drones, the album rejects the implicit contract that engagement-economy media demands. There is no hook arriving every fifteen seconds. Tracks unfold at the pace of geological processes. Music at this scale operates like a physical environment.",
    "site_id": "avantmusicnews",
    "crawl_status": "success"
  },
